ich, Nicholas [R-AK-At Large]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AK"},{"bioguideId":"B001291","fullName":"Rep. Babin, Brian [R-TX-36]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-07","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T18:37:30+00:00","id":"hr26-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-03","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-10","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Energy and Natural Resources."},"laws":[],"number":"26","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Energy","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"P000048","district":11,"fullName":"Rep. Pfluger, August [R-TX-11]","party":"R","state":"TX"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-03","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Protecting American Energy Production Act</strong></p><p>This bill prohibits the President from declaring a moratorium on the use of hydraulic fracturing unless Congress authorizes the moratorium. The bill also expresses the sense of Congress that states should maintain primacy&nbsp;(authority) for the regulation of hydraulic fracturing for oil and natural gas production on state and private lands.</p><p>Hydraulic fracturing, or fracking, is a process to extract underground resources such as oil or gas from a geologic formation by injecting water, a propping agent (e.g., sand), and chemical additives into a well under enough pressure to fracture the formation.</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-06T15:49:59Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Protecting American Energy Production Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-08T18:09:59Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-08T18:09:59Z"}
